        "original_id": "c39b4f59-6080-5158-b913-b159f6634d89",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Ted Kennedy, John F. Fitzgerald, John F. Kennedy, Rose Kennedy, M.T. McGreevy, M.J. Regan\n- Places: Doyle's Cafe, Boston\n- Organizations: Royal Rooters\n- Roles: Senator, Mayor, chairman, secretary, maternal grandfather, spiritual leader\n\nFacts:\n- John F. Fitzgerald was born on February 11, 1863, and died on October 2, 1950.\n- John F. Fitzgerald was an American politician, the father of Rose Kennedy, and the maternal grandfather of President John F. Kennedy.\n- John F. Fitzgerald served for a time as chairman of the Royal Rooters while he was Boston Mayor, and M.J. Regan was the secretary during that period.\n- M.T. \"Nuf Ced\" McGreevy was the spiritual leader of the Royal Rooters.\n- On St. Patrick's Day in 1988, Senator Ted Kennedy helped dedicate a new room at Doyle's Cafe to his maternal grandfather, John F. Fitzgerald.",
